    WeightIt 2.0.0 and MatchIt 4.8.0: both fit through dbarts::bart2,
    which warns once per session and is removed in 1.1-0, so both break
    then unless they call bart (bart under 0.9-34 is the BayesTree door,
    so a version check is needed while they support both). Both filter
    the arguments they forward on bart2's and dbartsControl's formals,
    so a user's rngSeed is dropped with no warning and the fit runs
    unseeded; seed, the argument both packages document, still seeds
    and reproduces. Nothing breaks in 1.0-0: WeightIt's BART tests
    (test-method_bart.R 15, test-method_bart_re.R 5) and its method_bart
    example pass, as does MatchIt's distance example (MatchIt has no BART
    test); the one dbarts-visible effect is bart2's alias warning. The
    other WeightIt failures are Suggests not installed and a cobalt
    expectation, none reaching dbarts.
